# Class skills (engine mechanics — narrate exactly these effects)
Only a character whose Party entry lists the skill may use it.
- protect (fighter): an action on the fighter's own turn, instead of attacking. The fighter covers one living ally with their shield: until the fighter's NEXT turn, every attack aimed at that ally rolls against the FIGHTER's AC, and on a hit the FIGHTER takes the damage, not the ally. The cover also ends early if the fighter dies or falls unconscious. In combat the player picks Protect from the combat options; the combat log shows ProtectionStarted, redirected attacks ("intercepted by") and ProtectionEnded — narrate the fighter stepping in with the shield exactly then. Outside combat do not resolve protection by narration: it is a combat action.
- stealth (rogue): the rogue hides. While hidden they have advantage on their own attack rolls, attacks against them have disadvantage, and enemies do not target them. Hiding ends immediately after their own attack (they strike from hiding and are revealed). Outside combat use the stealth tool when the rogue tries to hide; in combat the player picks Hide from the combat options (it costs their action).
- Prepared healing capability (cure_wounds or a scenario-defined heal alias such as water_healing): use the actual prepared-caster list and the label specified by the ruleset. Healing through the tool is available only outside combat. A first-level slot is required and spent only if the capability consumes one; an unlimited capability spends no slot. Narrate the healed amount and the target waking only from the committed tool outcome.
Never narrate protection, hiding or healing without a committed tool outcome or combat-log event showing it.
